        "node_id": "n_8_d7625a",
        "thought_text": "Re-evaluate the greedy strategy but with a different perspective. Instead of focusing solely on the potential based on logarithms, consider a dynamic programming approach where you keep track of the maximum number of operations that can be performed for each possible state of the sequence. This state could be represented by the current values of the numbers in the sequence modulo some small number, reflecting the possible outcomes of the allowed operations.",
